  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\U0001F50D Objective:\n\nTo separate a mixture of iron filings and sand
    using physical separation techniques.\n\n\U0001F4A1 Theory:\n\nA mixture is a
    combination of two or more substances that are not chemically combined.\n\nThese
    components can be separated by physical means based on their physical properties.\n\nIn
    this experiment, iron filings (magnetic) and sand (non-magnetic) are mixed together.\n\nA
    magnet can be used to attract and separate the iron filings from the sand.\n\nThis
    method is called magnetic separation.\n\n\U0001F9EA Apparatus Used:\n\u2022 Iron
    Filings\n\u2022 Sand\n\u2022 China Dish\n\u2022 Magnet\n\u2022 Collection Dishes\n\n\U0001F52C
    Procedure:\n\nPlace the mixture of iron filings and sand in a china dish.\n\nBring
    the magnet near the surface of the mixture.\n\nObserve the attraction of iron
    filings toward the magnet.\n\nSeparate the iron filings and collect them in a
    different dish.\n\nSand remains in the china dish, completing the separation.\n\n\u2705
    Observation:\n\nIron filings are attracted by the magnet.\n\nSand remains unaffected
    and separated in the dish.\n\n\U0001F4CC Conclusion:\n\nMagnetic separation is
    an effective method to separate a magnetic material from a non-magnetic one.\n\n\U0001F4D8
    Learning Outcomes:\n\n\u2022 Understand the concept of mixtures and separation
    techniques.\n\u2022 Identify magnetic and non-magnetic materials.\n\u2022 Learn
    how physical properties are used for separation.\n\u2022 Develop practical skills
    in handling lab apparatus."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d383cc1211c7a447bf206169c33c84c, type: 2}
