--- !u!114 &578660883
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 578660881}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\U0001F50D Objective:\r\nTo identify various metal ions by observing the
    characteristic flame color each produces during heating.\r\n\r\n\U0001F4A1 Theory:\r\n-
    When metal salts are heated in a flame, the electrons in the metal atoms get
    excited.\r\n- As these electrons return to their ground state, they emit light
    of specific wavelengths.\r\n- This emitted light appears as a flame of a distinct
    color, unique to each element.\r\n- This method is commonly used for identifying
    metal ions in qualitative analysis.\r\n\r\n\U0001F9EA Apparatus Used:\r\n\u2022
    Metal Salts (Strontium, Cesium, Sodium, Lithium)  \r\n\u2022 Nichrome Wire or
    Stick  \r\n\u2022 Lamp or Bunsen Burner  \r\n\u2022 Matchbox or Ignition Source 
    \r\n\u2022 Safety Tools (Goggles, Lab Stand)\r\n\r\n\U0001F52C Procedure:\r\n1.
    Light the lamp using a matchbox.\r\n2. Dip the stick into strontium salt and
    place it in the flame \u2014 observe the red color.\r\n3. Reheat the stick and
    dip it into cesium salt \u2014 observe the blue/violet flame.\r\n4. Repeat the
    process for sodium \u2014 observe the intense yellow flame.\r\n5. Continue for
    lithium \u2014 observe the crimson/red flame.\r\n6. Clean the stick between each
    test to avoid contamination.\r\n\r\n\u2705 Observation:\r\n\u2022 Strontium \u2192
    Bright Red Flame  \r\n\u2022 Cesium \u2192 Violet-Blue Flame  \r\n\u2022 Sodium
    \u2192 Golden Yellow Flame  \r\n\u2022 Lithium \u2192 Crimson Red Flame\r\n\r\n\U0001F4CC
    Conclusion:\r\nEach metal ion emits a characteristic flame color, which can be
    used to identify unknown samples.\r\n\r\n\U0001F4D8 Learning Outcomes:\r\n\u2022
    Understand how flame color relates to electron transitions.  \r\n\u2022 Gain
    hands-on experience in identifying metal ions.  \r\n\u2022 Learn proper flame
    test technique and observation.\r\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d383cc1211c7a447bf206169c33c84c, type: 2}
