--- !u!114 &979573714
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 979573712}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: ">> Objective:\n\nTo demonstrate the process of sublimation using Ammonium
    Chloride (NH\u2084Cl) and understand how certain substances transition directly
    from solid to gas without passing through the liquid phase.\n\n>> What is Sublimation?\n\nSublimation
    is a physical change in which a substance changes directly from a solid state
    to a gaseous state upon heating, bypassing the liquid phase.\nThis happens in
    substances with high vapor pressure at relatively low temperatures.\n\nExamples
    of substances that undergo sublimation:\n\nAmmonium Chloride (NH\u2084Cl)\n\nNaphthalene
    Balls\n\nIodine Crystals\n\nCamphor\n\n>> Materials Required:\n\nAmmonium Chloride
    (NH\u2084Cl)\n\nChina Dish\n\nWire Gauze\n\nTripod Stand\n\nInverted Funnel\n\nCotton
    Plug\n\nMatchbox or Bunsen Burner\n\nHeat Source\n\n>>Procedure :\n\nPlace NH\u2084Cl
    in a China Dish\nThe sublimating substance (NH\u2084Cl) is placed in the china
    dish.\n\nSet up the Wire Gauze and Tripod Stand\nThe china dish is placed on
    wire gauze over the stand for uniform heating.\n\nCover with an Inverted Funnel\nThe
    funnel helps to trap and guide the vapors.\n\nPlug the Funnel\u2019s Narrow End
    with Cotton\nThe cotton prevents vapor from escaping and helps with condensation.\n\nIgnite
    the Burner\nHeat the setup using a matchbox or burner.\n\nObserve the Sublimation\nNH\u2084Cl
    turns into vapor and re-solidifies as white crystals on the cooler funnel walls.\n\n\U0001F9E0>>
    Conclusion:\n\nAmmonium Chloride sublimates directly upon heating.\n\nThe crystalline
    deposit on the funnel proves the reversible physical change.\n\nThis experiment
    clearly shows the difference between physical and chemical changes.\n\n\U0001F4A1>>
    Learning Outcomes:\n\nUnderstand sublimation as a physical change.\n\nIdentify
    sublimating substances.\n\nLearn basic lab techniques.\n\nSee how sublimation
    can be used for purification processes.\n\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d383cc1211c7a447bf206169c33c84c, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -2519903747605655627, guid: 7d383cc1211c7a447bf206169c33c84c, type: 2}
