  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\U0001F50D Objective:\r\nTo observe the behavior of miscible and immiscible
    liquids and how they mix or separate when combined.\r\n\r\n\U0001F4A1 Theory:\r\n-
    Miscible liquids: are liquids that dissolve completely into each other, forming
    a uniform solution.\r\n- Immiscible liquids : do not mix and form separate layers
    due to differences in density and polarity.\r\n- Water and alcohol are miscible,
    while water and oil are immiscible.\r\n- Understanding this behavior is important
    in many real-life chemical and industrial processes.\r\n\r\n\U0001F9EA Apparatus
    Used:\r\n\u2022 Water  \r\n\u2022 Alcohol  \r\n\u2022 Oil  \r\n\u2022 Stirrer 
    \r\n\u2022 Beakers or Containers  \r\n\u2022 Arrows to Indicate Target Mixtures 
    \r\n\r\n\U0001F52C Procedure:\r\n1. Pour water into Beaker 1.\r\n2. Add alcohol
    into the same beaker.\r\n3. Stir the mixture using a stirrer \u2014 water and
    alcohol mix completely.\r\n4. Repeat with water and oil \u2014 observe separation
    after stirring.\r\n5. Add alcohol to oil \u2014 observe partial mixing, still
    immiscible.\r\n6. Stir again \u2014 observe how immiscible liquids retain separate
    layers.\r\n\r\n\u2705 Observation:\r\n\u2022 Water and alcohol form a clear,
    uniform mixture (miscible).  \r\n\u2022 Water and oil do not mix \u2014 they
    form layers (immiscible).  \r\n\u2022 Oil and alcohol also do not mix well.\r\n\r\n\U0001F4CC
    Conclusion:\r\n- Liquids like water and alcohol are **miscible** and mix uniformly. 
    \r\n- Liquids like water and oil are **immiscible**, forming separate layers. 
    \r\n- This experiment helps understand solubility and polarity differences between
    substances.\r\n\r\n\U0001F4D8 Learning Outcomes:\r\n\u2022 Understand the difference
    between miscible and immiscible liquids.  \r\n\u2022 Observe how polarity and
    density affect mixing.  \r\n\u2022 Learn how to interpret layering and solution
    formation.  \r\n\u2022 Gain practical skills in mixing and stirring techniques
    in the lab.\r\n"
