--- !u!114 &1694601856
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1694601854}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\U0001F50D Objective:\r\nTo determine the boiling point of ethyl alcohol
    (ethanol) using a simple laboratory setup.\r\n\r\n\U0001F4A1 Theory:\r\n- Every
    liquid has a specific temperature at which it boils and turns into vapor.\r\n-
    This is called the boiling point of the substance.\r\n- Ethyl alcohol (C\u2082H\u2085OH)
    is a volatile liquid, and its boiling point is approximately 78.5\xB0C at standard
    atmospheric pressure.\r\n- This experiment helps observe the boiling behavior
    of ethyl alcohol and measure its boiling point using a thermometer.\r\n\r\n\U0001F9EA
    Apparatus Used:\r\n\u2022 Beaker  \r\n\u2022 Boiling Tube  \r\n\u2022 Thermometer 
    \r\n\u2022 Ethyl Alcohol  \r\n\u2022 Matchbox or Heat Source  \r\n\u2022 Stand
    Setup and Fire Source\r\n\r\n\U0001F52C Procedure:\r\n1. Pour ethyl alcohol into
    the boiling tube.\r\n2. Place the boiling tube in a beaker containing water (water
    bath setup).\r\n3. Insert the thermometer into the tube.\r\n4. Heat the setup
    gently using a matchbox or fire source.\r\n5. Observe the thermometer reading
    while the alcohol heats and begins to boil.\r\n\r\n\u2705 Observation:\r\n- Ethyl
    alcohol starts boiling at approximately 78.5\xB0C.\r\n- Bubbles form as the alcohol
    converts from liquid to vapor.\r\n\r\n\U0001F4CC Conclusion:\r\n- The boiling
    point of ethyl alcohol is successfully determined using a thermometer and water
    bath setup.\r\n- The experiment shows how boiling point is a physical property
    that can be measured through controlled heating.\r\n\r\n\U0001F4D8 Learning Outcomes:\r\n\u2022
    Understand the concept of boiling point.  \r\n\u2022 Learn how to use laboratory
    apparatus.  \r\n\u2022 Observe physical changes during boiling.  \r\n\u2022 Understand
    the importance of uniform heating using a water bath."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
