--- !u!114 &1841808635
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1841808633}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\U0001F50D Objective:\nTo separate a mixture of naphthalene and sand using
    the sublimation method.\n\n\U0001F4A1 Theory:\n\nSublimation is a process in
    which a solid directly changes into its gaseous state upon heating, without passing
    through the liquid state.\n\nNaphthalene is a sublimable substance\u2014it changes
    directly from solid to vapor when heated.\n\nSand, being non-sublimable, remains
    in the container.\n\nThis difference in physical properties helps us separate
    the two components using sublimation.\n\n\U0001F9EA Apparatus Used:\n\u2022 China
    Dish\n\u2022 Funnel\n\u2022 Wire Gauze\n\u2022 Cotton Plug\n\u2022 Matchbox (Heat
    Source)\n\u2022 Burner Setup\n\u2022 Mixture of Sand and Naphthalene\n\n\U0001F52C
    Procedure:\n\nPlace the mixture of sand and naphthalene in a china dish.\n\nCover
    the china dish with a funnel.\n\nPlug the funnel mouth with cotton to prevent
    vapors from escaping.\n\nPlace the china dish on wire gauze and begin heating
    it gently.\n\nObserve the sublimation of naphthalene and its deposition on the
    inner walls of the funnel.\n\n\u2705 Observation:\n\nNaphthalene vaporizes and
    collects on the inner surface of the funnel as white crystals.\n\nSand remains
    in the china dish, confirming successful separation.\n\n\U0001F4CC Conclusion:\n\nThe
    experiment demonstrates the principle of sublimation as a method for separating
    a sublimable solid (naphthalene) from a non-sublimable solid (sand).\n\n\U0001F4D8
    Learning Outcomes:\n\u2022 Understand the process of sublimation.\n\u2022 Identify
    substances that undergo sublimation.\n\u2022 Learn how to apply sublimation for
    separation.\n\u2022 Observe physical changes in substances during heating.\n\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d383cc1211c7a447bf206169c33c84c, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -2519903747605655627, guid: 7d383cc1211c7a447bf206169c33c84c, type: 2}
